## SUMMARY: Issues Requiring Action Before Moving to Task 5+

### 🔴 Critical (Block progress)

| ID | File | Issue |
|---|---|---|
| 4-C | `config/settings.py` | `AUTH_USER_MODEL` not set — will cause irreversible DB state if migrations run first |
| 4-D | `config/asgi.py` | Missing `ProtocolTypeRouter` — WebSockets will never work |

### 🟠 High (Will cause errors at runtime)

| ID | File | Issue |
|---|---|---|
| 3-A | `docker-compose.yml` | Django running via `runserver` not `daphne` — ASGI/WebSocket won't work |
| 3-B | `docker-compose.yml` | MinIO health check uses `mc` which is not in the image — always fails |
| 4-A | `config/settings.py` | `django_celery_beat` missing from `INSTALLED_APPS` — celery-beat DB tables won't be created |
| 4-B | `config/settings.py` | `rest_framework_simplejwt.token_blacklist` missing — JWT blacklisting will throw errors |

### 🟡 Medium (Will cause subtle bugs)

| ID | File | Issue |
|---|---|---|
| 2-A | `.env.local` | Inline comment on `EMAIL_SERVICE` line may be parsed as part of the value |
| 2-B | `.env.local` | Missing `POSTGRES_*` and `REDIS_*` individual env vars used by `settings.py` |
| 3-C | `docker-compose.yml` | Django service's env vars don't come through properly for DB connection |

### 🟢 Low (Minor / cosmetic)

| ID | File | Issue |
|---|---|---|
| 3-D | `docker-compose.yml` | Typesense & Celery health checks are too weak (process check vs API check) |
| 4-E | `accounts/` | `views.py` and `urls.py` are placeholder stubs (expected, but noted) |

